WEBVTT

1
00:01:08,318 --> 00:01:11,405
NOTHING BETWEEN US

2
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,185
Don't say anything.

3
00:01:47,858 --> 00:01:49,985
<i>How did you get my room number?</i>

4
00:01:52,904 --> 00:01:54,197
I called the front desk.

5
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:03,206
<i>The first time you saw me...
Was it at the meeting?</i>

6
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:05,167
Yes.

7
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:08,795
<i>And what did you think?</i>

8
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,466
"That Mexican guy's got
really good skin."

9
00:02:16,845 --> 00:02:17,846
<i>And you?</i>

10
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:20,349
<i>When was the first time you saw me?</i>

11
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:26,271
<i>What did you think?</i>

12
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,026
I don't know.

13
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:34,237
<i>Many things.</i>

14
00:02:43,372 --> 00:02:44,790
<i>Are you close to the wall?</i>

15
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:58,804
Can you feel it?

16
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,226
<i>As if there were nothing between us.</i>

17
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:16,405
<i>I'm honest with her and with you</i>

18
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:22,035
<i>I love her, and I have forgotten you</i>

19
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:25,163
<i>If you...</i>

20
00:03:25,247 --> 00:03:28,375
<i>If you want, we'll be friends</i>

21
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:33,171
<i>I'll help you forget the past...</i>

22
00:03:33,255 --> 00:03:36,967
TWO DAYS EARLIER

23
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,929
<i>We still haven't received
the lab results.</i>

24
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:44,057
I think the most important thing
is to know where it happened,

25
00:03:44,141 --> 00:03:46,351
whether it was only in Bogotá
or somewhere else.

26
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:49,730
<i>Yes. Of course, the plant is in Bogotá.</i>

27
00:03:49,813 --> 00:03:51,898
<i>From there,
the whole country is supplied.</i>

28
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:55,485
<i>We're tracing it because apparently
it wasn't just one batch.</i>

29
00:03:56,027 --> 00:03:58,280
So it happened
in other places too, right?

30
00:03:58,697 --> 00:04:01,450
<i>We don't know yet.
We're focusing on Manizales</i>

31
00:04:01,783 --> 00:04:04,453
<i>because that's where most people
have gone to health centers.</i>

32
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:07,038
<i>But it's true
that there may be false positives</i>

33
00:04:07,122 --> 00:04:11,001
<i>and complaints meant only to harm us.
You know how it is, Guillermo.</i>

34
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:14,296
<i>We spoke with the ministry,
and everything's fine there.</i>

35
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,006
<i>There won't be any problems.</i>

36
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:18,425
<i>But now it's spreading
across all the media</i>

37
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:20,761
<i>and, although it's not official yet,</i>

38
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:24,347
<i>they're talking about 5000 cases,
but the batch is over 25,000.</i>

39
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:27,934
<i>That's why the sooner we deal with this,
the better,</i>

40
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:30,937
<i>so we can avoid a wave of lawsuits
and a market crash,</i>

41
00:04:31,354 --> 00:04:34,357
<i>which is surely what will happen
if we do nothing.</i>

42
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:35,984
Sure.

43
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:38,028
And by the time we see each other,

44
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:40,947
things will have escalated a bit,
won't they?

45
00:04:42,491 --> 00:04:45,827
I promised company shares

46
00:04:45,911 --> 00:04:51,458
to every damn nurse and doctor
I ran into at the hospital.

47
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:57,297
Even today we're still getting
lawsuits at the office.

48
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,049
Isn't that right, Doc?

49
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:02,135
And what they charge me!

50
00:05:03,261 --> 00:05:08,058
Do you know why God
made snakes before lawyers?

51
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,142
No.

52
00:05:09,226 --> 00:05:11,061
He needed the practice.

53
00:05:13,897 --> 00:05:14,981
Thank you.

54
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:20,320
Three cardiorespiratory arrests,
but dying was never part of my plans.

55
00:05:20,946 --> 00:05:22,405
Not that day.

56
00:05:23,156 --> 00:05:26,952
And in that damn hospital,
just two floors up,

57
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:32,791
my daughter was giving birth
to the most important child of my life.

58
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,251
Junior.

59
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,461
Happy birthday.

60
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:44,803
I hope you have a very fulfilling life.
You know I adore you.

61
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:50,475
And you also know that the word "lose"
doesn't exist in my vocabulary.

62
00:05:57,691 --> 00:05:59,442
- What is it?
- Turn it on.

63
00:06:02,863 --> 00:06:03,864
No way.

64
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:14,374
- Did you already know?
- What?

65
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:15,458
Did you know?

66
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:20,964
Father-in-law!

67
00:06:21,798 --> 00:06:22,799
How are you?

68
00:06:22,883 --> 00:06:25,385
What a gift. Thank you so much.

69
00:06:25,719 --> 00:06:28,346
Hey, Richard told me
about what happened in Colombia.

70
00:06:28,430 --> 00:06:32,183
It's a real ordeal,
but you can make the most of it.

71
00:06:32,267 --> 00:06:35,395
Yes, we're talking now.
I'm checking what...

72
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:36,479
Where to?

73
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:37,981
Yes.

74
00:06:39,149 --> 00:06:40,901
No. Not now.

75
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:43,403
No, no! This is madness right here!

76
00:06:57,334 --> 00:06:59,419
I mean, really, it's like a spaceship.

77
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:01,212
- And the boom is...
- Really?

78
00:07:01,296 --> 00:07:02,964
- What's that?
- Yes.

79
00:07:04,925 --> 00:07:06,801
- I'm going to check it out.
- Yes.

80
00:07:07,761 --> 00:07:11,723
BUENOS AIRES, ARGENTINA

81
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:15,852
Coca.

82
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:25,153
Where is it?

83
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:31,159
- Hello.
- <i>Hi, Mechi.</i>

84
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:33,828
- <i>Did I wake you? Sorry about the time.</i>
- No. What happened?

85
00:07:33,912 --> 00:07:35,789
<i>The CEO's assistant called me
at 04:00 AM.</i>

86
00:07:35,872 --> 00:07:38,917
<i>Do you think someone
should call me at 04:00 AM...?</i>

87
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,127
The CEO's assistant called you. And?

88
00:07:41,211 --> 00:07:42,754
<i>Emergency meeting.</i>

89
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:45,215
<i>You must be in Mexico tomorrow
for a regional matter.</i>

90
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:48,218
What? Tomorrow in Mexico? Why?

91
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:50,345
<i>Do you remember
Daiana went to Colombia?</i>

92
00:07:50,428 --> 00:07:52,347
<i>She's a friend.
She told me not to say anything.</i>

93
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:55,475
- <i>Do you remember her?</i>
- Maga, please. What?

94
00:07:56,017 --> 00:07:57,978
<i>There was a case of food poisoning</i>

95
00:07:58,061 --> 00:07:59,938
<i>from Mamá Emilia tomato cans
in Colombia.</i>

96
00:08:00,021 --> 00:08:03,149
<i>Regional meeting.
You fly tonight. Two nights.</i>

97
00:08:03,233 --> 00:08:05,318
<i>Go with carry-on luggage.
You board at 10:00 PM.</i>

98
00:08:05,402 --> 00:08:07,404
<i>You can hang out
in the VIP lounge before.</i>

99
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:10,073
- <i>You're flying business class.</i>
- In business class?

100
00:08:10,865 --> 00:08:13,159
But I run the poorest area
of the company,

101
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,369
as if they'd send me.

102
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:17,247
I've been emailing
for a week to get toner.

103
00:08:18,081 --> 00:08:20,333
Emerging Latin America
is Leo Darner, not me.

104
00:08:20,417 --> 00:08:24,004
<i>He's in Nordelta on psychiatric leave.
Between us, do you remember</i>

105
00:08:24,087 --> 00:08:26,339
<i>the community dining hall
Barriguita Contenta?</i>

106
00:08:26,423 --> 00:08:29,259
<i>He sent the donations to a Chinese
supermarket near his place.</i>

107
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:32,846
- <i>Well, I'm sending you an Uber now.</i>
- Wait.

108
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:34,973
- <i>I figured you're going to the airport.</i>
- But tell them

109
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:37,350
I need to make another stop first.

110
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:39,769
<i>Where do you need to stop? Tell me.</i>

111
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:49,988
Damn dog!

112
00:09:07,756 --> 00:09:08,757
And Frida?

113
00:09:11,134 --> 00:09:12,886
- Frida!
- Don't shout.

114
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:15,138
- You're going to wake her up.
- It's 7:15.

115
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,141
Where are you going?

116
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:20,894
To Mexico. I just found out.
But I'm flying business.

117
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:23,104
If they give you a blanket, take it.

118
00:09:23,188 --> 00:09:26,149
Here. This week
you won't need to make copies.

119
00:09:26,232 --> 00:09:28,318
Great. Were they in your bedroom?

120
00:09:30,153 --> 00:09:31,946
- What about school?
- Cut it out.

121
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,323
It's 7:15 AM, Frida.

122
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:38,328
I let her skip. We stayed up late
working on the project.

123
00:09:40,038 --> 00:09:42,248
- You need to ask both of us.
- You're never here.

124
00:09:42,332 --> 00:09:46,920
You call me and ask me. Go get changed.
I don't care that you slept two hours.

125
00:09:47,003 --> 00:09:48,338
Kato, take her.

126
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:24,249
Give them away, sell them,
but get the computers out of here.

127
00:10:24,332 --> 00:10:26,292
In two months, we'll use them all.

128
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:29,796
Where's the digital camera?
The one we bought in Ciudad del Este.

129
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:33,133
I don't know.
You still have 40 boxes to open.

130
00:10:33,216 --> 00:10:34,968
- Read it and tell me what you think.
- I can't.

131
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,302
- I can't. I have to go.
- Take it.

132
00:10:36,386 --> 00:10:37,971
- I'm coming out.
- Read it.

133
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,889
- Get Coca off the couch.
- Go ahead.

134
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:47,272
Where's the hair remover?
Where do you keep it?

135
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:48,439
My mom has it.

136
00:10:50,358 --> 00:10:51,526
Come here for a second.

137
00:10:52,902 --> 00:10:55,113
We'll have to record
our conversations again.

138
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:58,158
- Why?
- Why? Because I'm fed up.

139
00:10:58,241 --> 00:11:01,202
- Relax a little.
- No. Do you know where I'm going now?

140
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:03,872
Damn dog hair all over me.

141
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,045
In front of her?

142
00:11:11,129 --> 00:11:13,423
Yes.
"She doesn't like going to school."

143
00:11:13,756 --> 00:11:17,010
He's always coming up with nonsense.
He imagines ridiculous businesses.

144
00:11:17,385 --> 00:11:19,095
He hasn't made a buck in ages,

145
00:11:19,179 --> 00:11:20,930
and now we're living
at my mother-in-law's.

146
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:23,975
It's complicated. Very complicated.

147
00:11:26,269 --> 00:11:28,313
- Is it called "cryptocurrencies"?
- Yes.

148
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:31,316
He bought 10 computers.
He brought a bunch of Venezuelan kids.

149
00:11:31,399 --> 00:11:34,235
I have no problem with Venezuelans.
I really like the kids.

150
00:11:34,319 --> 00:11:37,405
But they killed the power on the block.
The neighbors hate us.

151
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:42,285
Short story? I've got all the computers
lying around in the dining room.

152
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:45,205
- It's complicated, right?
- Very.

153
00:11:45,288 --> 00:11:48,458
Give me a second. Delfi, could you
please bring me the protein shake

154
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:51,169
and Mechi's papers for her to sign?
Thanks.

155
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:55,757
Mechi, we've talked it through
completely. We already know how it is.

156
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,842
We know how to proceed in these cases.

157
00:11:57,926 --> 00:11:58,968
Thanks, honey.

158
00:12:00,011 --> 00:12:01,012
All right.

159
00:12:01,804 --> 00:12:03,765
We had already talked about this.

160
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:07,143
Just a second, I'll be right with you.
This call is really important.

161
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:10,104
Hello, doctor. How are you doing?

162
00:12:10,772 --> 00:12:13,233
Honey, just sign
where it says your name,

163
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:15,902
and we'll take care of the rest, okay?

164
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:17,737
Tell me, doctor. I'm listening.

165
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:20,865
Yes, the mediation is next week,

166
00:12:20,949 --> 00:12:23,868
but I need you to help me
with your client's attitude.

167
00:12:26,829 --> 00:12:27,830
Come on.

168
00:12:34,379 --> 00:12:36,339
JUDICIARY

169
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:12,208
I'M LEAVING, WHERE ARE YOU?

170
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:16,796
WORKING OUT. COMING BACK LATE?
CHICKEN FOR DINNER.

171
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:35,189
REGIONAL MEETING.
I PUT IT ON THE CALENDAR.

172
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,250
Thank you.

173
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,401
Welcome...

174
00:14:46,386 --> 00:14:48,846
- Can I help you with something?
- No, thank you.

175
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:51,766
My golf clubs are back there. Thanks.

176
00:15:43,985 --> 00:15:46,404
Getting connected is easy.

177
00:15:46,904 --> 00:15:50,825
Look, the confirmation arrived,
the recall is done.

178
00:15:51,159 --> 00:15:52,827
- Okay, recall.
- Okay.

179
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:54,954
- That's good.
- Yes.

180
00:15:55,037 --> 00:15:58,291
According to their version,
there is so much production demand

181
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,960
that they had to start reducing
exposure times,

182
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,128
as they told me at the plant.

183
00:16:02,211 --> 00:16:03,838
- Just kidding!
- No, I don't think so.

184
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,381
- Just kidding.
- It's weird.

185
00:16:05,715 --> 00:16:06,883
It's unbelievable.

186
00:16:06,966 --> 00:16:08,134
- Damn it.
- Sorry.

187
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:11,012
They'll send him the information
as soon as they have it.

188
00:16:14,223 --> 00:16:16,893
From all the branches.
That's their version.

189
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:20,438
They'll call you later
about the curry issue.

190
00:16:21,063 --> 00:16:22,106
It's still pending.

191
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:42,168
2014,
National Dream Company from Shanghai.

192
00:16:43,127 --> 00:16:47,965
2017, a Conservative MP
in the UK Parliament

193
00:16:48,049 --> 00:16:50,092
tested positive
for methamphetamines.

194
00:16:55,097 --> 00:17:00,186
2020, bribery and sewage failures
struck southern Chile.

195
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:09,153
I'm going to make a prediction.
Anything could happen.

196
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:11,239
But I'm sure of one thing:

197
00:17:11,322 --> 00:17:14,367
We'll come out of this
stronger than we went in.

198
00:17:14,450 --> 00:17:15,868
It's up to us.

199
00:17:16,244 --> 00:17:20,122
All the cases
we've shown you ended well.

200
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:23,876
How? By acting immediately.

201
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:27,880
That's why it's so important
we decided to meet here in person.

202
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:31,133
If we do things right,

203
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:35,972
tomorrow the market could open
about two points higher.

204
00:17:36,806 --> 00:17:39,225
If I were you, I'd buy shares today.

205
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:44,105
Guillermo.

206
00:17:44,188 --> 00:17:49,777
Sorry, it's just that I'm right here
buying some shares. There you go.

207
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,320
I bought some for you too, Steve.

208
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,864
No, sorry. Bad joke.

209
00:17:55,283 --> 00:17:58,286
We truly value all the effort
you and your team

210
00:17:58,369 --> 00:18:00,788
are putting into addressing
this situation,

211
00:18:00,871 --> 00:18:03,207
but my recommendation is

212
00:18:03,291 --> 00:18:06,961
that we should not make such
a rushed decision.

213
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:10,840
If we don't say something soon,
we'll be harmed, dear Guillermo.

214
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:13,718
Yes, but it's not
necessary to respond.

215
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:17,388
We can... We have 24 hours.

216
00:18:17,972 --> 00:18:20,933
We can develop a plan together.

217
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,437
Not rely on an external advisor
to hand us a magic recipe.

218
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:27,064
This cannot wait. We have to be agile.

219
00:18:27,148 --> 00:18:29,442
The weekend is coming,
and each day could get worse.

220
00:18:29,859 --> 00:18:32,361
We must respond to our clients
and to the market.

221
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:33,863
Exactly, in that order.

222
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:37,283
First with our clients,
and then with the market.

223
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:41,871
We can apologize,
we can develop a long-term plan.

224
00:18:41,954 --> 00:18:44,123
- How long has it been since we...?
- Guillermo, please.

225
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,458
Yes, sorry.

226
00:18:45,875 --> 00:18:48,044
Well, we've identified
what the problem is.

227
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:50,046
It's an outbreak caused by...

228
00:18:56,010 --> 00:18:57,678
- Escherichia coli?
- Exactly.

229
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,890
The plant is back
to normal operation.

230
00:19:00,973 --> 00:19:04,393
Fortunately, only a very small
percentage of cases can be severe.

231
00:19:05,019 --> 00:19:11,025
So far, of the 300 "supposed" victims,
none show apparent severity.

232
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:14,236
In fact, we have been attentive
to their families,

233
00:19:14,320 --> 00:19:16,155
providing them with our products.

234
00:19:16,238 --> 00:19:17,823
But wasn't it 5000?

235
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:21,035
I remind you
that this information is confidential.

236
00:19:21,827 --> 00:19:24,997
You're receiving a document
with the media plan to be executed.

237
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:26,332
There you will find

238
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:31,128
the press release text
tailored for each news network.

239
00:19:31,212 --> 00:19:33,381
Let's take a five-minute break.

240
00:20:11,794 --> 00:20:12,795
Pay attention.

241
00:20:13,129 --> 00:20:16,465
"Grupo Alicabo, the largest
food company on the continent,

242
00:20:16,799 --> 00:20:18,467
seems to be overcoming
the minor setback

243
00:20:18,801 --> 00:20:22,179
it suffered in recent days
with the batch of affected products.

244
00:20:22,263 --> 00:20:26,016
Foreseeing an increase in its profits
for the next quarter,

245
00:20:26,100 --> 00:20:28,811
it will surpass previous estimates."

246
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:32,106
<i>...for the next quarter,
it will surpass previous estimates.</i>

247
00:20:32,815 --> 00:20:36,986
<i>This is because the market also rewards
Alicabo's commitment to ecology.</i>

248
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:43,284
<i>The company is committed
to reducing greenhouse gas emissions</i>

249
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:45,286
<i>through strict industry controls...</i>

250
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:47,496
- Cheers!
- Congratulations!

251
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,165
Looks like it worked, right?

252
00:20:50,124 --> 00:20:51,459
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

253
00:20:58,174 --> 00:21:01,385
<i>...complaints from some users
who noticed...</i>

254
00:21:06,932 --> 00:21:09,393
<i>And a fury arose within me
that energized me.</i>

255
00:21:09,727 --> 00:21:12,062
<i>It quickened my heartbeat
and drove me to action.</i>

256
00:21:12,146 --> 00:21:16,942
<i>Is it logical to continue encouraging
livestock and agrotoxic production,</i>

257
00:21:17,777 --> 00:21:20,863
<i>knowing it devastates
entire communities and ecosystems?</i>

258
00:21:21,363 --> 00:21:23,115
<i>After the Amazon fires,</i>

259
00:21:23,199 --> 00:21:26,285
<i>we will reach two degrees
within the next decade.</i>

260
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:30,498
<i>Planetary transformation phenomena
will not be stopped by law.</i>

261
00:21:50,893 --> 00:21:53,771
Hello, Ana. How are you?
It's been such a long time. I'm Mechi.

262
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:58,734
By chance, I came across your talk,
and I thought it was incredible.

263
00:21:59,068 --> 00:22:00,194
I loved it.

264
00:22:02,071 --> 00:22:05,407
Congratulations, I'm so proud.

265
00:22:08,911 --> 00:22:10,871
Everything you achieved and...

266
00:22:11,914 --> 00:22:15,835
I know it wasn't easy for you.
So it has double merit.

267
00:22:18,003 --> 00:22:21,423
Well, maybe I didn't know
how to be there...

268
00:22:30,432 --> 00:22:31,725
PERFECT SKIN
SAVE THE PLANET!

269
00:22:31,809 --> 00:22:33,394
IT'S NEVER TOO LATE!
RECYCLING CHANGES EVERYTHING!

270
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:34,478
NATURAL SECRET.
FRIDA MESSAGE

271
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:37,940
Frida, what are you doing
awake at this hour?

272
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:42,361
Honey, come on. Go to sleep, please.
You've got school tomorrow. Off you go.

273
00:22:47,950 --> 00:22:51,871
Kato, could you ask Frida to go to bed
since she has to get up early tomorrow?

274
00:22:51,954 --> 00:22:52,955
Would that be okay?

275
00:23:11,932 --> 00:23:12,933
Help!

276
00:23:13,976 --> 00:23:15,352
Please, Kato, answer the phone.

277
00:23:15,853 --> 00:23:18,981
Come on, answer the phone, Kato.

278
00:23:39,877 --> 00:23:40,878
Miss!

279
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:49,011
Crunchy candies
are perfect for a scare.

280
00:23:53,182 --> 00:23:55,851
What is the protocol?
Do they take us to a shelter?

281
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:58,103
Where to? What?

282
00:23:58,687 --> 00:24:00,147
What's so funny? Everything moved!

283
00:24:00,230 --> 00:24:03,108
No, relax. Everything's fine, okay?

284
00:24:03,192 --> 00:24:04,693
But couldn't a tsunami happen?

285
00:24:05,444 --> 00:24:08,447
Who would think of putting
a tsunami meeting point on the beach?

286
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:13,953
I completely agree with that.
It's ridiculous that this is here.

287
00:24:14,036 --> 00:24:15,746
Don't worry about the quake.

288
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:21,043
I'm Mexican, and we Mexicans
have a developed seismometer.

289
00:24:21,752 --> 00:24:26,423
And here I've got an app
that shows the quake's location,

290
00:24:27,383 --> 00:24:31,845
its magnitude, and any tsunami alert.

291
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:38,268
The fright I got, my God.

292
00:24:42,731 --> 00:24:44,400
- What are you watching?
- I don't know.

293
00:24:46,193 --> 00:24:48,362
Lately it's the only way
I can get myself to sleep.

294
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:50,823
Welcome to the club.

295
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:54,410
That's how it starts,
then come the anxiolytics,

296
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:58,247
and three months later
you end up here on the beach cot.

297
00:24:59,832 --> 00:25:02,918
I'd rather the beach cot
than ending up in a cell,

298
00:25:03,002 --> 00:25:04,878
locked up for making people sick.

299
00:25:04,962 --> 00:25:08,048
Locked up and sleepless,
just look at that. What a mix.

300
00:25:08,716 --> 00:25:09,758
A real mess.

301
00:25:10,426 --> 00:25:13,095
Like your regional manager,
stuck in a big mess.

302
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:14,763
- Looks that way.
- Yes.

303
00:25:15,097 --> 00:25:17,099
But they had to send someone,
and they sent me.

304
00:25:20,102 --> 00:25:23,272
And what's with that airline T-shirt?
Are they sponsoring you?

305
00:25:23,939 --> 00:25:26,191
No. A lifetime flying economy,

306
00:25:26,275 --> 00:25:29,111
broken bathroom,
foot stench, coffin seat.

307
00:25:29,194 --> 00:25:31,780
Once I finally get business class,
they lose my suitcase.

308
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:36,952
But they gave me a T-shirt
and a toiletry bag full of junk.

309
00:25:37,745 --> 00:25:41,040
Not bad, right?
The T-shirt is pretty nice.

310
00:25:41,415 --> 00:25:42,416
What am I doing here?

311
00:25:48,797 --> 00:25:50,924
I used to have a sustainable venture
with my friend.

312
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:53,802
We were doing well,
but then, at some point, we weren't...

313
00:25:55,095 --> 00:25:58,098
I needed the money,
and this company called me, and...

314
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:01,977
I proposed a bunch of changes,
switching the materials.

315
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:04,313
They did nothing.

316
00:26:06,315 --> 00:26:08,317
And here we are, wrecking the planet

317
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:10,235
and, on top of that,
poisoning ourselves.

318
00:26:12,321 --> 00:26:15,908
But do you know this is the first case
of poisoning in Alicabo's history?

319
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:18,911
Yes, in 85 years, it's the first.

320
00:26:18,994 --> 00:26:20,913
- I don't believe it.
- I swear.

321
00:26:20,996 --> 00:26:23,916
Most likely,
the Colombians got poisoned

322
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,959
because of poor sterilization.

323
00:26:26,710 --> 00:26:29,004
- Yes.
- And do you know why? To cut costs.

324
00:26:30,214 --> 00:26:32,091
I know the numbers have to add up.

325
00:26:32,174 --> 00:26:35,928
And if they're sending us all here,
it's because the numbers add up.

326
00:26:36,011 --> 00:26:38,305
- Yes.
- But for the clients and us workers,

327
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:39,389
the numbers don't add up.

328
00:26:45,813 --> 00:26:46,814
Yes.

329
00:26:47,189 --> 00:26:51,151
I don't think it's healthy
trying to sleep on the beach this late.

330
00:26:56,198 --> 00:26:57,199
Give me your hand.

331
00:26:57,866 --> 00:26:59,785
Excuse me. This might hurt.

332
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:04,123
- Do you feel it?
- Yes.

333
00:27:05,916 --> 00:27:06,917
Here?

334
00:27:07,793 --> 00:27:08,794
Dude.

335
00:27:11,713 --> 00:27:12,840
How do you know this?

336
00:27:14,133 --> 00:27:15,134
My dad.

337
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:18,804
For years
he'd lock himself in a dark room.

338
00:27:21,056 --> 00:27:22,850
In time we learned it was tinnitus.

339
00:27:22,933 --> 00:27:25,352
That's what I've got.

340
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:28,188
And how did you find out?

341
00:27:29,148 --> 00:27:31,066
Last night at the meeting. Excuse me.

342
00:27:31,817 --> 00:27:35,445
Hold on tight here.
Squeeze hard. Don't let go.

343
00:27:36,238 --> 00:27:37,865
The key is to be consistent.

344
00:27:41,994 --> 00:27:43,162
Sorry.

345
00:27:43,245 --> 00:27:44,246
Hello.

346
00:27:45,414 --> 00:27:47,124
No, the call started accidentally.

347
00:27:48,458 --> 00:27:51,211
Yes, twice at this hour.
I'll call you tomorrow.

348
00:27:54,965 --> 00:27:56,091
- Are you leaving?
- Yes.

349
00:27:56,175 --> 00:27:58,927
No. Why don't we grab a drink?

350
00:27:59,928 --> 00:28:01,805
- At this hour?
- Yes.

351
00:28:02,681 --> 00:28:03,849
Just one. For the shock.

352
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:07,895
Do you think the media plan will work?

353
00:28:08,270 --> 00:28:11,732
Honestly, it's hard to tell
how the markets will react, my friend.

354
00:28:12,107 --> 00:28:13,901
We just don't know.
We can't predict it.

355
00:28:20,908 --> 00:28:21,909
Yes.

356
00:28:29,791 --> 00:28:33,045
I'm sure it was a singer...
A male singer.

357
00:28:33,795 --> 00:28:35,172
I think it was a Mexican song.

358
00:28:42,054 --> 00:28:45,349
A song my mom used to play
every Sunday, ten times over.

359
00:28:46,099 --> 00:28:49,853
Recently divorced, she'd belt it out
while cleaning the house in a negligee,

360
00:28:49,937 --> 00:28:51,396
half-naked in front of my friends.

361
00:28:52,022 --> 00:28:54,149
I hated it, but it made her happy.

362
00:28:54,233 --> 00:28:57,110
But which Mexican singer?
A bit more info, right?

363
00:28:57,194 --> 00:28:58,820
There are thousands.

364
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:01,198
- Of course.
- Well.

365
00:29:02,658 --> 00:29:06,787
- Like that, really Mexican.
- Something more specific?

366
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,414
- It's kind of romantic.
- Of course.

367
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:15,254
No, I have no idea. I don't know.
And what's a negli...? What? Neglig...

368
00:29:15,337 --> 00:29:17,214
- Negligee? Like a robe.
- Yes.

369
00:29:18,006 --> 00:29:19,424
Why is it called that?

370
00:29:20,259 --> 00:29:24,263
Negligee. Like... I don't know.

371
00:29:24,346 --> 00:29:29,059
No way! I can't believe it.
Just look at that!

372
00:29:31,186 --> 00:29:32,771
- Absinthe?
- Yes.

373
00:29:32,854 --> 00:29:34,773
You want to cut off your ear?

374
00:29:34,856 --> 00:29:39,152
No, just a mild trip, that's all.
What do you think? Should we go for it?

375
00:29:39,236 --> 00:29:41,446
No. I don't know. I've never tried.

376
00:29:42,406 --> 00:29:45,409
Well, I can't imagine
a better setting, buddy.

377
00:29:45,742 --> 00:29:48,078
If we're going to prison,

378
00:29:48,161 --> 00:29:50,789
let's go
with the Green Fairy by our side.

379
00:29:52,249 --> 00:29:56,295
Let's see... Here's the water.
Perfect! That's it.

380
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:01,967
- So, your first time?
- Yes.

381
00:30:02,050 --> 00:30:06,305
Okay. I'll make them
kind of student-style, okay?

382
00:30:08,348 --> 00:30:09,349
Here.

383
00:30:12,477 --> 00:30:13,478
Take it.

384
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:16,189
Right there. Slowly, okay?

385
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,150
You've got to drink it slowly.

386
00:30:22,279 --> 00:30:23,280
Okay, then...

387
00:30:31,413 --> 00:30:35,083
<i>I'm honest with her and with you</i>

388
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:40,881
<i>I love her, and I've forgotten you</i>

389
00:30:42,424 --> 00:30:45,927
<i>If you want, we'll be friends</i>

390
00:30:46,762 --> 00:30:47,763
<i>I will...</i>

391
00:32:22,274 --> 00:32:24,025
- <i>Morning!</i>
- What happened, Catriel?

392
00:32:24,109 --> 00:32:26,862
<i>Hello, Mechi. How are you?
Nice day over there?</i>

393
00:32:27,279 --> 00:32:29,322
I'm in a hurry. Is everything okay?

394
00:32:29,781 --> 00:32:32,159
<i>No, everything's fine over here.
Crazy heat...</i>

395
00:32:32,242 --> 00:32:34,786
<i>Well, not everything's fine,
the internet's down.</i>

396
00:32:34,870 --> 00:32:37,789
- And what can I do from here?
- <i>I wanted to ask you...</i>

397
00:32:37,873 --> 00:32:40,125
- You went back to mining.
- <i>No, nothing like that.</i>

398
00:32:40,208 --> 00:32:42,377
<i>Frida has to turn in
a school assignment.</i>

399
00:32:42,461 --> 00:32:44,796
<i>Can you give me
the Novacel's customer number?</i>

400
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:47,382
<i>I call tech support,
I give them the address, the email,</i>

401
00:32:47,466 --> 00:32:49,426
<i>and those jerks
tell me it doesn't apply.</i>

402
00:32:49,509 --> 00:32:52,387
- <i>It's insane. I'm losing it.</i>
- Maybe it's because we have Sintel?

403
00:32:55,056 --> 00:32:56,057
<i>Sintel?</i>

404
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:58,894
<i>Maybe. I don't know. Are you sure?</i>

405
00:33:00,437 --> 00:33:02,772
- <i>Are you sure?</i>
- Yes, Catriel.

406
00:33:03,398 --> 00:33:05,192
- <i>I thought that...</i>
- Hold on.

407
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,945
- Hello.
- <i>Good morning.</i>

408
00:33:09,029 --> 00:33:11,823
<i>Just a reminder
that you need to check out before 10.</i>

409
00:33:11,907 --> 00:33:13,074
Thanks, yes.

410
00:33:14,743 --> 00:33:18,955
Yes, Catriel, Sintel. Username, my ID.
Password, Frida's birthday.

411
00:33:19,331 --> 00:33:21,833
I'll confirm when I'm back,
so you can pick me up.

412
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:26,087
- <i>Okay. I'm still going to call...</i>
- No, don't call, don't do anything.

413
00:33:26,171 --> 00:33:29,341
- Remember what happened last time.
- <i>Last time I understood how it was...</i>

414
00:33:33,762 --> 00:33:35,847
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

415
00:33:47,901 --> 00:33:50,904
At a certain age, coffee
isn't good for you. It's Kryptonite.

416
00:33:50,987 --> 00:33:52,781
Are you the guy from Mexico?

417
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:56,117
- Excuse me.
- Go ahead.

418
00:33:56,201 --> 00:33:59,788
- I didn't hear when you left.
- Not even when I came?

419
00:34:00,247 --> 00:34:02,249
I don't know what you're talking about.

420
00:34:02,332 --> 00:34:04,793
- Sorry, maybe I just imagined it.
- Yes.

421
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:11,967
How does this go on?

422
00:34:13,802 --> 00:34:16,805
Well, we've just had breakfast

423
00:34:17,430 --> 00:34:19,975
and we tell everyone
we're going to buy cigarettes.

424
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:22,936
And that's it. Live it up.

425
00:34:23,853 --> 00:34:24,854
I don't smoke.

426
00:34:26,106 --> 00:34:27,399
Seriously, how does it go on?

427
00:34:31,236 --> 00:34:33,947
No, that's it. We're all going home.

428
00:34:34,906 --> 00:34:36,825
The media campaign worked quite well.

429
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:41,413
All the shares, the likes,
the "responding," as they call it.

430
00:34:41,496 --> 00:34:42,497
All of that's pretty good.

431
00:34:43,415 --> 00:34:48,003
We don't know how stocks will open,
but Steve said that's it.

432
00:34:48,086 --> 00:34:51,047
Mrs. Batista.
The airline brought your suitcase.

433
00:34:52,299 --> 00:34:55,677
That T-shirt. We've got to frame it.

434
00:34:56,344 --> 00:34:57,721
- This way.
- Thank you.

435
00:35:05,520 --> 00:35:09,190
DESCRIPTION

436
00:35:21,244 --> 00:35:24,080
Excuse me, but I had promised it
to the manager in Panama.

437
00:35:26,291 --> 00:35:29,252
We could say that, so far,
our relationship has been a success.

438
00:35:29,336 --> 00:35:32,964
Yes. You've got a mouth
that tells the truth.

439
00:35:34,049 --> 00:35:38,136
- And so? Well, what do we do?
- Do we quit while we're ahead?

440
00:35:38,219 --> 00:35:39,220
Bye, Guillermo.

441
00:35:41,097 --> 00:35:45,352
No emails, no private messages
to get attention. Okay?

442
00:35:45,435 --> 00:35:47,437
Yes, that's fine with me. It's okay.

443
00:35:57,238 --> 00:35:58,239
Steve.

444
00:35:59,240 --> 00:36:00,825
Guillermo, safe travels.

445
00:36:02,744 --> 00:36:03,828
See you soon, Ale.

446
00:36:03,912 --> 00:36:05,246
- Have a good trip.
- Thank you.

447
00:36:13,129 --> 00:36:17,092
- Long trip?
- Going back home. What a relief.

448
00:36:23,973 --> 00:36:28,269
- Why is it so noisy? What's going on?
- God. What happened? It's dropping.

449
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,153
ALICABO IN FREE FALL

450
00:36:37,237 --> 00:36:40,448
<i>The drop in Alicabo's shares
is not a good sign.</i>

451
00:36:41,449 --> 00:36:44,494
<i>The decisions
made by the current CEO have failed</i>

452
00:36:44,577 --> 00:36:47,372
<i>to give consumers
the necessary confidence.</i>

453
00:36:48,164 --> 00:36:49,165
<i>On the other hand,</i>

454
00:36:49,249 --> 00:36:53,503
<i>lawsuits over the poisoning cases
continue to reach the courts.</i>

455
00:36:54,087 --> 00:36:56,548
Today, the Alicabo family needs you.

456
00:36:57,340 --> 00:37:00,593
With the truth,
without resorting to media gimmicks.

457
00:37:01,636 --> 00:37:05,473
As you can see, that figure
falling short of our predictions

458
00:37:05,557 --> 00:37:08,643
compels us to form a crisis committee.

459
00:37:13,022 --> 00:37:14,023
Just call here and you're all set.

460
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:18,653
All good.

461
00:37:19,612 --> 00:37:22,407
Now it's going to work! No, sorry.

462
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:26,286
That's it. Now we're good.

463
00:37:32,417 --> 00:37:34,669
<i>The CEO's departure is also a sign.</i>

464
00:37:35,170 --> 00:37:36,671
<i>And perhaps it's time to step back</i>

465
00:37:36,755 --> 00:37:39,299
<i>and see how Alicabo
can defend its market value.</i>

466
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:42,051
<i>I'm sure it's something circumstantial,</i>

467
00:37:42,135 --> 00:37:44,637
<i>but I'd rather stay out than in,
and, in any case,</i>

468
00:37:44,721 --> 00:37:47,348
<i>come back in once management
resolves the problems</i>

469
00:37:47,432 --> 00:37:49,642
<i>with their Mamá Emilia brand.</i>

470
00:37:50,226 --> 00:37:52,562
<i>Rumors about the possible resignation
of Steve Díaz,</i>

471
00:37:52,645 --> 00:37:55,482
<i>the current CEO of Alicabo,
are growing stronger,</i>

472
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:57,400
<i>and the markets have opened lower.</i>

473
00:37:57,484 --> 00:37:59,319
<i>The future does not look promising.</i>

474
00:37:59,402 --> 00:38:02,155
<i>And unless the course changes,
nothing good can happen.</i>

475
00:38:02,238 --> 00:38:05,617
<i>...a very negative reaction of 90%.</i>

476
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:09,078
<i>There was also a small group
inside of that percent</i>

477
00:38:09,162 --> 00:38:11,122
<i>that physically assaulted our goods.</i>

478
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:14,667
We're still together, right?

479
00:38:19,214 --> 00:38:20,548
Tomorrow makes it three days.

480
00:38:21,382 --> 00:38:24,594
I'd have to sort out a couple of things
in Buenos Aires first.

481
00:38:24,677 --> 00:38:26,095
Have you been married long?

482
00:38:28,056 --> 00:38:31,518
Eighteen years,
but the last ones were endless.

483
00:38:38,483 --> 00:38:39,484
Let's see.

484
00:38:41,027 --> 00:38:42,362
I never look good in photos.

485
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:45,448
No, don't delete it. Come on.

486
00:38:46,324 --> 00:38:47,325
Look.

487
00:38:48,368 --> 00:38:49,494
Is that your daughter?

488
00:38:51,287 --> 00:38:52,288
Frida.

489
00:38:53,206 --> 00:38:55,917
A 15-year-old teenager. Beautiful.

490
00:38:56,000 --> 00:38:57,710
But she argues with me
about everything.

491
00:38:58,211 --> 00:39:00,004
She doesn't let a single thing slide.

492
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:03,091
I don't feel
like sucking up to her anymore.

493
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:05,093
Suck up to her?

494
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:08,388
- It sounds ugly.
- Yes, it's really strange.

495
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:13,017
Did you know
I promised her a new phone?

496
00:39:15,687 --> 00:39:17,689
Do you know any place
where I could buy it?

497
00:39:19,107 --> 00:39:22,402
At the... Yes, at the mall.
I'll take you.

498
00:39:22,485 --> 00:39:23,611
- Of course.
- Yes.

499
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:29,742
How beautiful.

500
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:33,121
And you?

501
00:39:35,456 --> 00:39:39,752
José María. Chemita. He's 17.

502
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:43,089
Honestly, he's a great guy.
Super chill.

503
00:39:44,507 --> 00:39:46,175
He's named after his grandfather.

504
00:40:23,171 --> 00:40:24,464
Hold on.

505
00:40:25,673 --> 00:40:27,759
You're going to break your hip, Mexico.

506
00:40:28,551 --> 00:40:30,136
And I'll end up with cystitis.

507
00:40:31,554 --> 00:40:34,515
Hold on.
What if we use the right technique?

508
00:40:34,599 --> 00:40:36,517
The right technique? Which one?

509
00:40:36,601 --> 00:40:39,228
Sorry. My phone is ringing a lot.

510
00:40:39,312 --> 00:40:40,647
Okay. Yes.

511
00:40:50,531 --> 00:40:51,532
Sorry.

512
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,493
Hello, my love. What happened?

513
00:40:54,410 --> 00:40:56,496
<i>Nothing, it's me. Listen.</i>

514
00:40:56,579 --> 00:40:59,582
<i>We're outside the airport,
the parking is a rip-off.</i>

515
00:40:59,666 --> 00:41:00,667
<i>Are you out yet?</i>

516
00:41:01,501 --> 00:41:07,256
No, no, Kato. They didn't tell you.
I asked them to let you know.

517
00:41:07,340 --> 00:41:08,341
<i>About what?</i>

518
00:41:09,008 --> 00:41:12,679
Everything got complicated
with the poisoning and we had to stay.

519
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,597
<i>I haven't slept.
I asked them to tell you.</i>

520
00:41:14,681 --> 00:41:16,265
Did you ask them to tell me?

521
00:41:16,349 --> 00:41:18,476
Look at that.
No, of course, it's top secret.

522
00:41:18,559 --> 00:41:22,146
I bet you can't even send
a voice message while you're peeing.

523
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:24,273
<i>You're right. This is madness.</i>

524
00:41:24,357 --> 00:41:26,693
<i>I'm not making excuses,
but you're right. Sorry.</i>

525
00:41:26,776 --> 00:41:29,570
Could you repeat all that
so I can record it?

526
00:41:29,654 --> 00:41:31,698
And make sure
the "you're right" is clear.

527
00:41:31,781 --> 00:41:34,367
- <i>Are you on speakerphone?</i>
- No.

528
00:41:38,037 --> 00:41:40,456
Kato, it's the first
free minute I've had, you know?

529
00:41:40,540 --> 00:41:42,625
I'm sorry, really. Believe me.

530
00:41:42,709 --> 00:41:45,294
And besides, I just paid off the loan.

531
00:41:45,712 --> 00:41:47,714
Next month you're up.
I've done my part.

532
00:41:48,047 --> 00:41:50,508
I don't know how you'll do it,
sell the computers, the dogs...

533
00:41:50,591 --> 00:41:52,427
<i>Yes, forget it. Don't worry.</i>

534
00:41:53,094 --> 00:41:54,554
<i>Hi, Mom. Turn on the camera.</i>

535
00:42:01,144 --> 00:42:03,104
- Hi, dear.
- <i>Show us the hotel.</i>

536
00:42:04,731 --> 00:42:07,233
No, I can't, sweetheart,
because I'm around people.

537
00:42:08,234 --> 00:42:11,237
<i>We have a couple of questions
about Dad's presentation next week.</i>

538
00:42:12,071 --> 00:42:13,072
<i>Do you have a minute?</i>

539
00:42:13,698 --> 00:42:15,450
Yes, go ahead, yes.

540
00:42:15,533 --> 00:42:18,327
<i>But with good vibes, okay?
Not trying to change everything.</i>

541
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:21,289
- <i>Go ahead. Just like we practiced.
- Alright.</i>

542
00:42:22,582 --> 00:42:26,294
<i>Do you have trouble finding
a mate for your dog?</i>

543
00:42:26,377 --> 00:42:31,424
<i>This is simple:
Alzaditos, Tinder for pets.</i>

544
00:42:32,425 --> 00:42:33,676
<i>The claw was Frida's idea.</i>

545
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:36,763
Yes, it's really funny.
And how are you going to monetize it?

546
00:42:37,346 --> 00:42:38,347
We're on it.

547
00:42:38,431 --> 00:42:41,726
Sponsors, a seven-day trial
and an annual membership.

548
00:42:42,060 --> 00:42:45,271
You need to be the new Instagram
for people to spend money on ads.

549
00:42:45,354 --> 00:42:47,231
<i>That's true, but not quite like that.</i>

550
00:42:47,315 --> 00:42:50,777
<i>In this case, the key is
that your clients are your partners.</i>

551
00:42:51,444 --> 00:42:54,697
<i>So you get paid again
from the future sale of the puppies.</i>

552
00:42:54,781 --> 00:42:57,033
No, they'll crucify you
if you sell a dog.

553
00:42:57,116 --> 00:42:58,284
It doesn't work that way.

554
00:42:58,367 --> 00:43:01,662
Okay, thank you. Always trying
to improve everything. Take it.

555
00:43:01,746 --> 00:43:05,541
No, come on. Wait.
Not like that. Hold on. Stop.

556
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,376
No, no. Frida.

557
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:12,757
Dude, you can't always see everything
in a negative way.

558
00:43:14,092 --> 00:43:16,219
I don't care. The idea is great.

559
00:43:16,302 --> 00:43:19,639
Next week I'll pitch it
to some startup investors,

560
00:43:20,306 --> 00:43:22,225
but Frida worked hard on this.

561
00:43:22,308 --> 00:43:25,645
She's really into it.
Just fake it in front of her, at least.

562
00:43:25,728 --> 00:43:27,146
<i>Frida should be in school,</i>

563
00:43:27,647 --> 00:43:29,398
not wasting time with her dad's ideas.

564
00:43:30,483 --> 00:43:34,362
<i>And you should stop giving orders,
complain less,</i>

565
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:36,155
<i>and spend more time with your daughter.</i>

566
00:43:38,074 --> 00:43:39,075
I talked to the lawyer.

567
00:43:40,326 --> 00:43:45,665
Again. Another fight, another mess
at work, another "let's split up."

568
00:43:46,040 --> 00:43:48,209
Do it, Mechi. Do it already,

569
00:43:48,543 --> 00:43:52,171
but if I were you, I'd wait a few months
until Alzaditos gets going.

570
00:43:52,255 --> 00:43:54,757
Are you messing with me? Kat...

571
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:01,305
Sorry.

572
00:44:18,573 --> 00:44:22,285
That's usually how it goes.
This is the third one we've had.

573
00:44:22,368 --> 00:44:26,205
- Did you know this, Guillermo?
- No, how would I know?

574
00:44:26,706 --> 00:44:31,043
It's the third one.
They got rid of the first two.

575
00:44:34,046 --> 00:44:37,258
As you know, the markets
have reacted negatively,

576
00:44:37,341 --> 00:44:40,219
and unfortunately,
Steve is no longer with the company.

577
00:44:41,137 --> 00:44:43,222
Let's take a break
for a couple of hours

578
00:44:43,306 --> 00:44:46,267
while the board
appoints an interim CEO.

579
00:44:46,601 --> 00:44:49,270
As soon as I have the schedule
for the next meeting,

580
00:44:49,353 --> 00:44:51,522
I'll let you know. Thank you.

581
00:44:53,107 --> 00:44:54,442
Are you interested in the group?

582
00:44:55,318 --> 00:44:57,278
- Yes.
- There are two.

583
00:44:57,361 --> 00:44:59,447
Okay, we can go.

584
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:02,992
Yes, right.

585
00:45:04,035 --> 00:45:06,996
- That's all.
- Let's check.

586
00:45:23,012 --> 00:45:27,099
This one has 3 percent milk
and a bit of wheat protein.

587
00:45:34,273 --> 00:45:35,566
This one's super easy!

588
00:45:35,650 --> 00:45:40,571
Refried pinto beans, made in Sinaloa,
no preservatives. This is the one.

589
00:45:41,572 --> 00:45:43,574
Yes. The truth is
it's the only good one.

590
00:45:43,658 --> 00:45:45,451
Pass me a little water, will you?

591
00:45:49,622 --> 00:45:50,623
Let's see...

592
00:45:55,461 --> 00:45:56,545
How tasty, but...

593
00:45:56,629 --> 00:45:59,548
Let's do one more,
but this time you're going to smell it.

594
00:45:59,632 --> 00:46:00,633
Okay.

595
00:46:06,097 --> 00:46:07,390
Is that it? There?

596
00:46:09,100 --> 00:46:13,145
- What is it? Bet you can't.
- Wait, wait. Let me see.

597
00:46:14,563 --> 00:46:16,649
This is guacamole.
It's made from guaca...

598
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:18,109
- Yes!
- Wait.

599
00:46:18,192 --> 00:46:21,404
It's got lemon, and they only make it
that way in Panama,

600
00:46:21,487 --> 00:46:24,240
because it's made
for the U.S. market. They love it.

601
00:46:24,323 --> 00:46:26,075
- Panama!
- Really?

602
00:46:26,158 --> 00:46:27,660
- How can that be?
- That's it.

603
00:46:27,994 --> 00:46:29,328
- How can it be?
- Did you see?

604
00:46:31,414 --> 00:46:34,417
- Is that your phone or mine?
- Do you know any Javiera?

605
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:39,255
Shit.

606
00:46:45,553 --> 00:46:46,554
I'll be back.

607
00:46:56,022 --> 00:46:58,107
What's up? How's it going?

608
00:46:58,190 --> 00:47:00,526
- <i>Hello. How's everything over there?</i>
- Hello.

609
00:47:01,694 --> 00:47:04,697
Sorry. I was in a meeting,
so I couldn't answer.

610
00:47:05,156 --> 00:47:06,282
<i>In a meeting?</i>

611
00:47:06,365 --> 00:47:08,034
- Yes.
- <i>What's up with your style?</i>

612
00:47:08,117 --> 00:47:12,621
Yeah. They gave us all
some T-shirts here.

613
00:47:13,205 --> 00:47:14,707
You know how those things are.

614
00:47:15,082 --> 00:47:16,292
- <i>That's cool.</i>
- Yes.

615
00:47:16,375 --> 00:47:18,711
<i>Hey, did you see what a beauty?</i>

616
00:47:19,420 --> 00:47:21,672
- <i>What's up? It's impressive.</i>
- What's up, son?

617
00:47:22,006 --> 00:47:25,509
<i>There'd be a room left
for an office or something.</i>

618
00:47:25,593 --> 00:47:28,721
- <i>Or maybe a gym?
- A gym could work too.</i>

619
00:47:29,055 --> 00:47:31,724
<i>Mom, you have to show him the lake.
It's amazing.</i>

620
00:47:32,224 --> 00:47:34,477
- <i>I could have my nights out there.
- Sure.</i>

621
00:47:34,560 --> 00:47:38,022
<i>And look where it is. That's my Dad's!</i>

622
00:47:40,066 --> 00:47:42,401
<i>We're close, but not that close.</i>

623
00:47:43,235 --> 00:47:44,528
- <i>What do you think?</i>
- You know what?

624
00:47:44,612 --> 00:47:46,489
It's really pretty,

625
00:47:46,572 --> 00:47:49,325
but why don't we talk about it
when we meet?

626
00:47:49,408 --> 00:47:54,121
<i>You know how this is, Memo.
Besides, it's a really good price.</i>

627
00:47:54,205 --> 00:47:55,164
Yes, but...

628
00:47:55,247 --> 00:47:56,499
- <i>Hello, Memo.</i>
- What's up?

629
00:47:57,208 --> 00:48:00,461
<i>Look, if when I die
there's money left in the bank,</i>

630
00:48:00,544 --> 00:48:04,340
<i>it means I miscalculated my accounts.
It has to stay in the family.</i>

631
00:48:04,423 --> 00:48:05,549
<i>We lose nothing.</i>

632
00:48:06,467 --> 00:48:07,468
Alright.

633
00:48:08,177 --> 00:48:12,223
<i>Well, I'm off, it's time
to eat here. Think about it.</i>

634
00:48:12,306 --> 00:48:17,436
Yes. See you later.
So then, we'll talk about it, right?

635
00:48:18,187 --> 00:48:20,398
- <i>But we will talk about it!</i>
- Yes, of course.

636
00:48:20,481 --> 00:48:22,525
- <i>You already heard grandpa.</i>
- Yes. Bye, son.

637
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:24,568
- <i>Bye.</i>
- I'm leaving.

638
00:48:24,652 --> 00:48:25,653
<i>Bye.</i>

639
00:48:28,197 --> 00:48:30,491
- All good?
- Yes.

640
00:48:32,034 --> 00:48:33,119
Yes, all good.

641
00:48:46,465 --> 00:48:47,633
Did they scold you?

642
00:48:48,634 --> 00:48:50,302
And we can't keep playing?

643
00:48:54,557 --> 00:48:55,599
Did they scold me?

644
00:48:56,559 --> 00:48:58,060
Sorry, I imagined it.

645
00:48:58,978 --> 00:49:00,146
Did you imagine it?

646
00:49:06,110 --> 00:49:07,278
What do you imagine?

647
00:49:14,493 --> 00:49:15,661
What do you imagine about me?

648
00:49:16,328 --> 00:49:17,538
- Really?
- Yes, really.

649
00:49:22,585 --> 00:49:26,130
You get home
around five or six, more or less.

650
00:49:26,505 --> 00:49:28,424
A perfect, minimalist house.

651
00:49:29,049 --> 00:49:34,555
You walk in, there's a huge library,
full of design books you'll never open.

652
00:49:35,389 --> 00:49:37,308
Your wife hears you coming in,

653
00:49:37,391 --> 00:49:40,186
but instead of calling out,
she WhatsApps you to come up.

654
00:49:40,269 --> 00:49:42,021
Then you go upstairs,

655
00:49:42,521 --> 00:49:45,024
family vacation photos line the walls.

656
00:49:45,691 --> 00:49:49,111
In your hand you carry
a little gift for her.

657
00:49:49,195 --> 00:49:51,447
It's what she told you
to get at the duty free shop,

658
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:53,115
since you wouldn't know what to buy.

659
00:49:54,116 --> 00:49:57,286
You enter your room,
she's tidying her closet,

660
00:49:57,369 --> 00:50:00,164
piles of clothes,
but she never knows what to wear.

661
00:50:00,998 --> 00:50:05,961
She greets you with a smile,
you share a little kiss. She's lovely.

662
00:50:06,921 --> 00:50:08,297
She puts on too much makeup, though.

663
00:50:08,923 --> 00:50:11,300
Your son is there too,
with his best friend.

664
00:50:11,634 --> 00:50:15,513
His name is...
You never remember his name.

665
00:50:15,596 --> 00:50:18,682
Well, never mind.
The nanny calls for dinner just then.

666
00:50:18,766 --> 00:50:20,226
Every Thursday they eat chicken.

667
00:50:21,185 --> 00:50:22,186
And that's it.

668
00:50:22,937 --> 00:50:25,356
You talk a bit about the news,
the weather, and not much else.

669
00:50:33,531 --> 00:50:35,282
- And that's it?
- That's it.

670
00:50:45,167 --> 00:50:47,127
Alright, see you in a bit. Okay?

671
00:51:14,238 --> 00:51:15,781
DID YOU EAT BREAKFAST?

672
00:51:20,452 --> 00:51:22,371
- Good morning.
- Hello, good morning.

673
00:51:22,454 --> 00:51:24,123
- Hello, good morning.
- Hello.

674
00:51:24,707 --> 00:51:26,292
- Not bad.
- I'm on a diet.

675
00:51:26,375 --> 00:51:28,377
- Congratulations.
- Exceptional.

676
00:51:29,044 --> 00:51:30,629
- What did you think?
- Are you okay?

677
00:51:31,088 --> 00:51:32,673
- Let's see.
- Great choice.

678
00:51:33,716 --> 00:51:34,717
- Thank you.
- See you later.

679
00:51:35,134 --> 00:51:36,635
- Good morning.
- What will you be having?

680
00:51:38,304 --> 00:51:41,348
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

681
00:51:55,571 --> 00:51:59,575
<i>The market welcomed the resignation
of our former CEO, Steve Díaz.</i>

682
00:52:00,159 --> 00:52:01,410
<i>The new crisis plan includes</i>

683
00:52:01,493 --> 00:52:04,496
<i>the company's acknowledgment
of its mistake</i>

684
00:52:04,580 --> 00:52:07,750
<i>and a consumer-focused
recovery strategy.</i>

685
00:52:08,083 --> 00:52:10,628
<i>Vanesa will be in charge
of the strategy</i>

686
00:52:10,711 --> 00:52:13,005
<i>while we appoint our CEO.</i>

687
00:52:13,756 --> 00:52:15,924
<i>We're working with consultants.</i>

688
00:52:16,008 --> 00:52:18,636
<i>Soon they'll present
innovative proposals</i>

689
00:52:19,178 --> 00:52:23,349
<i>to reach all media outlets.</i>

690
00:52:23,432 --> 00:52:24,433
Do I know you?

691
00:52:24,516 --> 00:52:26,185
<i>...that has such an impact...</i>

692
00:52:26,268 --> 00:52:28,437
- Can I help you?
- What?

693
00:52:28,520 --> 00:52:30,314
You heard me, is there a problem?

694
00:52:30,397 --> 00:52:31,690
Yes, my problem is you.

695
00:52:32,232 --> 00:52:35,194
Do you know what they do
with the food your family wastes?

696
00:52:37,071 --> 00:52:39,073
- They throw it away.
- Speak English.

697
00:52:39,156 --> 00:52:41,408
Your country uses
more resources than others,

698
00:52:41,492 --> 00:52:42,701
but the planet is everyone's.

699
00:52:43,035 --> 00:52:47,164
Doesn't matter, because later you start
a war and get them back, right?

700
00:52:47,247 --> 00:52:49,208
You understand or not, damn Yankee?

701
00:52:52,127 --> 00:52:53,379
They're Germans.

702
00:53:06,392 --> 00:53:09,228
- Excuse me.
- Yes, ma'am, how can I help you?

703
00:53:09,311 --> 00:53:11,271
No. Not help, Esperanza.

704
00:53:11,355 --> 00:53:14,066
I want to apologize.
I don't usually react like that,

705
00:53:14,400 --> 00:53:16,735
but they come here
with their first-world attitude.

706
00:53:17,069 --> 00:53:18,737
At home they recycle,
here we're monkeys.

707
00:53:19,363 --> 00:53:22,700
- Sure, ma'am.
- Actually, I need something.

708
00:53:23,033 --> 00:53:26,537
Do you know a place
that sells used iPhones?

709
00:53:27,162 --> 00:53:29,581
- Compu Palace?
- Compu Palace.

710
00:53:30,082 --> 00:53:33,377
<i>Let me tell you the story
of what's about to happen.</i>

711
00:53:33,460 --> 00:53:37,339
<i>It's a dirt-poor town in the middle
of the Colombian mountains and jungle.</i>

712
00:53:37,423 --> 00:53:38,424
<i>It's Sunday.</i>

713
00:53:38,507 --> 00:53:40,592
<i>Families are getting together.</i>

714
00:53:40,676 --> 00:53:42,094
<i>Picture four kids.</i>

715
00:53:42,428 --> 00:53:45,514
<i>Four boys, between ages of 5 and 12.</i>

716
00:53:46,598 --> 00:53:49,643
<i>Now, they've got some cash
stashed in their socks</i>

717
00:53:49,727 --> 00:53:53,689
<i>because their mother's sent them out
to buy their favorite thing:</i>

718
00:53:53,772 --> 00:53:57,359
<i>three cans of Mamá Emilia tomato sauce.</i>

719
00:53:58,527 --> 00:54:01,530
<i>Now they jump over puddles,
they run across open fields,</i>

720
00:54:01,613 --> 00:54:03,532
<i>they climb wire fences,</i>

721
00:54:03,615 --> 00:54:05,701
<i>picking up stray dogs along the way.</i>

722
00:54:06,034 --> 00:54:08,662
<i>All of this
just to get to the town's store.</i>

723
00:54:08,996 --> 00:54:12,166
<i>One of them proposes a shortcut</i>

724
00:54:12,249 --> 00:54:13,667
<i>crossing dead tracks.</i>

725
00:54:13,751 --> 00:54:17,379
<i>The rest follow, but just as they're
about to cross the tracks,</i>

726
00:54:17,463 --> 00:54:21,216
<i>they all fall into an old well
that hasn't been filled properly.</i>

727
00:54:21,300 --> 00:54:23,677
<i>Hours will go by
before anybody finds them.</i>

728
00:54:24,762 --> 00:54:28,557
<i>Eventually, everybody will flock
over there: their parents, the press,</i>

729
00:54:28,640 --> 00:54:32,352
<i>rescue teams, neighbors,
relatives from out of town,</i>

730
00:54:32,436 --> 00:54:33,687
<i>the local priest.</i>

731
00:54:33,771 --> 00:54:36,607
<i>Everybody and their mother, literally.</i>

732
00:54:37,357 --> 00:54:40,652
<i>The news will be covered
by hundreds of media outlets.</i>

733
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:43,572
<i>Reporters will inform
that feeding them is a problem,</i>

734
00:54:43,655 --> 00:54:45,532
<i>that it is almost impossible
to get them out</i>

735
00:54:45,616 --> 00:54:49,077
<i>because the well is too narrow
and a mudslide has blocked the way in.</i>

736
00:54:49,661 --> 00:54:52,080
<i>The world will empathize.</i>

737
00:54:52,414 --> 00:54:54,541
<i>Everybody will be up
watching the live feed.</i>

738
00:54:54,625 --> 00:54:57,085
<i>Every detail counts.</i>

739
00:54:58,045 --> 00:55:00,339
<i>Then, when emotions
are at their highest,</i>

740
00:55:00,422 --> 00:55:04,676
<i>we'll see a rescue worker pulling
a string used to reach the boys.</i>

741
00:55:05,260 --> 00:55:09,348
<i>Live, the world will see
that the string is tied to the lid...</i>

742
00:55:09,431 --> 00:55:10,432
No way.

743
00:55:10,516 --> 00:55:14,561
<i>...of one of the Mamá Emilia sauce cans
that the kids bought two days earlier.</i>

744
00:55:16,188 --> 00:55:18,190
<i>That will be the key</i>

745
00:55:18,607 --> 00:55:20,526
<i>to knowing that the kids are safe,</i>

746
00:55:21,735 --> 00:55:23,529
<i>that they've been able
to feed themselves.</i>

747
00:55:24,154 --> 00:55:27,366
<i>They live thanks to this amazing sauce!</i>

748
00:55:28,742 --> 00:55:31,745
- <i>Everybody will go wild with joy.</i>
- What a moron.

749
00:55:32,371 --> 00:55:34,748
<i>Just picture the celebration,
the emotion!</i>

750
00:55:50,180 --> 00:55:53,725
<i>I think I knew it before you.
Well deserved...</i>

751
00:55:55,769 --> 00:55:59,523
<i>The happy family.
I told you so, didn't I?</i>

752
00:56:01,233 --> 00:56:05,529
<i>Here's your regional manager
waiting for the future CEO at hole one.</i>

753
00:56:06,113 --> 00:56:07,114
<i>Where are you?</i>

754
00:56:08,198 --> 00:56:11,410
<i>Wow, Guillermo.
What a joy. Congratula...</i>

755
00:56:15,622 --> 00:56:16,623
Right.

756
00:56:49,448 --> 00:56:50,532
Future CEO!

757
00:56:50,616 --> 00:56:52,576
- He showed up! Let's play.
- Let's play.

758
00:56:52,659 --> 00:56:54,286
- Let's play!
- Come on.

759
00:56:54,703 --> 00:56:56,288
Been waiting an hour, man.

760
00:56:56,997 --> 00:56:59,458
Guillermo. Come here, man!

761
00:57:10,177 --> 00:57:11,511
See you again at six.

762
00:57:12,304 --> 00:57:13,388
Bye for now.

763
00:57:43,293 --> 00:57:44,336
Why don't you sleep?

764
00:57:46,380 --> 00:57:48,298
Should we... go in?

765
00:57:49,091 --> 00:57:50,092
Come with me.

766
00:57:55,472 --> 00:57:57,140
It's...

767
00:58:00,227 --> 00:58:01,436
that buzzing.

768
00:58:55,073 --> 00:58:56,074
Hi there!

769
00:58:58,535 --> 00:58:59,619
- Hello.
- Hi.

770
00:59:00,078 --> 00:59:01,079
How's it going?

771
00:59:01,580 --> 00:59:02,581
How are you, sweetheart?

772
00:59:03,290 --> 00:59:04,583
- Fine.
- Is school okay?

773
00:59:04,666 --> 00:59:06,251
- Yes.
- Perfect.

774
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:08,086
Denise, a friend.

775
00:59:08,170 --> 00:59:09,212
- Hi.
- Hi.

776
00:59:38,200 --> 00:59:39,201
Go to sleep.

777
00:59:40,202 --> 00:59:41,286
You need to rest.

778
00:59:42,454 --> 00:59:45,415
Yes.

779
00:59:50,504 --> 00:59:53,256
- Thanks.
- There. Lie down.

780
00:59:53,340 --> 00:59:54,591
- Here?
- Yes, here.

781
00:59:59,096 --> 01:00:01,223
Excuse me. Thank you.

782
01:00:02,307 --> 01:00:05,310
- So, honey, how was school?
- Really good.

783
01:00:05,393 --> 01:00:07,604
Yeah?
Lots of homework for tomorrow?

784
01:00:08,063 --> 01:00:09,231
Yes, too much.

785
01:00:09,689 --> 01:00:13,485
- Too much. What do you have? Math?
- English.

786
01:00:22,327 --> 01:00:23,662
And your friends?

787
01:00:23,745 --> 01:00:26,623
- My friends didn't come.
- They didn't?

788
01:00:28,333 --> 01:00:31,169
- Did they tell you?
- They went to the beach.

789
01:00:52,816 --> 01:00:55,193
- Do they have an iPhone 12?
- I don't know.

790
01:00:55,527 --> 01:00:57,195
Don't want to give her the latest.

791
01:00:57,279 --> 01:00:59,239
I think it's important
she values things.

792
01:01:06,371 --> 01:01:09,541
Come everyone!

793
01:01:09,624 --> 01:01:12,419
This is where you'll find everything!

794
01:01:14,379 --> 01:01:15,547
You said it's here?

795
01:01:18,717 --> 01:01:22,470
Esperanza. You won't believe it,
but I don't have any change.

796
01:01:22,554 --> 01:01:25,056
At the hotel we don't use cash. Sorry.

797
01:01:25,765 --> 01:01:28,351
I'll find you later
at the hotel and give it to you.

798
01:01:28,435 --> 01:01:30,645
- It's fine, ma'am. Forget it.
- Thank you.

799
01:01:35,150 --> 01:01:37,402
- Hey, blondie. Need a taxi?
- No.

800
01:01:38,111 --> 01:01:39,112
Thanks.

801
01:01:41,156 --> 01:01:43,533
What do you need?
Just tell me, I'll help.

802
01:01:44,409 --> 01:01:45,410
Compu Palace?

803
01:01:46,411 --> 01:01:48,121
- Here? Thanks.
- Yes.

804
01:01:53,752 --> 01:01:54,753
Buenos Aires?

805
01:01:56,254 --> 01:02:00,008
The Chacarita neighborhood, right?
A mess.

806
01:02:00,091 --> 01:02:01,218
Married?

807
01:02:01,301 --> 01:02:03,595
I'm on my third marriage, you know.

808
01:02:04,429 --> 01:02:05,639
Complicated? No.

809
01:02:06,014 --> 01:02:09,434
But I'll confess something to you.
I miss the first one.

810
01:02:10,185 --> 01:02:11,519
She understood me the most.

811
01:02:12,187 --> 01:02:13,521
Are you looking for an iPhone?

812
01:02:14,439 --> 01:02:18,777
Well, I wouldn't trust
buying it out here. They're open.

813
01:02:19,611 --> 01:02:22,614
Inside I've got someone
who can get it cheaper,

814
01:02:23,114 --> 01:02:24,491
and they're closed.

815
01:02:24,574 --> 01:02:27,535
- If you want, I'll talk to him.
- But is it Compu Palace?

816
01:02:27,619 --> 01:02:29,537
Friend,
here everything is Compu Palace.

817
01:02:30,121 --> 01:02:33,041
Look, it's all the same.
Follow me. I'll take you.

818
01:02:36,628 --> 01:02:39,381
Out here, honestly,
I don't trust buying.

819
01:02:39,464 --> 01:02:41,716
Everything's open.
You could get robbed, you know?

820
01:02:42,425 --> 01:02:44,803
Inside, it's a legit place.

821
01:02:45,262 --> 01:02:47,430
No strings attached.
Come on in. Look.

822
01:02:51,393 --> 01:02:53,520
They've got an eleven, really good.

823
01:02:53,603 --> 01:02:55,730
Five hundred bucks.
Killer price, friend.

824
01:02:55,814 --> 01:02:58,441
A bargain.
Plus, they're my buddies.

825
01:02:58,525 --> 01:03:00,652
Give me 400,
I'll go in and bargain for you.

826
01:03:00,986 --> 01:03:02,237
- Four hundred?
- Yes.

827
01:03:02,320 --> 01:03:03,571
And the battery's okay?

828
01:03:05,198 --> 01:03:08,660
Well, it's a gift for my daughter.

829
01:03:11,162 --> 01:03:12,163
I'll be back.

830
01:03:30,307 --> 01:03:33,268
He wants more money. 550, the bastard.

831
01:03:33,351 --> 01:03:35,103
- But up ahead, there's a place where...
- No, no.

832
01:03:35,186 --> 01:03:37,522
No, no. No need.
I'd rather come back another day.

833
01:03:37,605 --> 01:03:38,690
- Thank you.
- Alright.

834
01:03:40,191 --> 01:03:42,652
Hey, no.
That's not the money I gave you.

835
01:03:43,069 --> 01:03:45,613
What are you saying, friend?
You got something to tell me?

836
01:03:46,698 --> 01:03:48,658
What's wrong with you?
I just went in and out.

837
01:03:49,159 --> 01:03:50,744
- Are you crazy?
- They're fake.

838
01:03:52,620 --> 01:03:54,205
You got something to say?

839
01:03:56,041 --> 01:03:59,586
Look, if I were you,
I'd leave the way I came.

840
01:04:01,254 --> 01:04:03,423
Nothing's happening here, okay?

841
01:04:14,434 --> 01:04:16,644
<i>It's been 48 hours since the incident,</i>

842
01:04:16,728 --> 01:04:20,231
<i>and still no certainty
about how the rescue will work.</i>

843
01:04:21,191 --> 01:04:23,735
<i>Some say digging a parallel shaft
could be the solution,</i>

844
01:04:24,235 --> 01:04:28,239
<i>but they fear the walls might collapse
once digging begins.</i>

845
01:04:28,573 --> 01:04:31,159
<i>We don't know
the children's condition,</i>

846
01:04:31,242 --> 01:04:34,037
<i>but apparently their health is stable.</i>

847
01:04:34,454 --> 01:04:40,460
<i>It's news that shocks us all.
Truly unfortunate.</i>

848
01:04:40,543 --> 01:04:43,338
- Hi.
- <i>Are you busy? Just a second.</i>

849
01:04:43,421 --> 01:04:47,175
<i>Did you see I got the meeting
with investors to pitch Alzaditos?</i>

850
01:04:47,258 --> 01:04:51,346
<i>In Marketing class we're seeing
it's good to go with a story</i>

851
01:04:51,429 --> 01:04:54,182
<i>that defines the DNA
of the idea, you know?</i>

852
01:04:54,265 --> 01:04:56,518
<i>Something personal.
Can I read you something?</i>

853
01:04:56,601 --> 01:04:58,520
No, not now, I'm busy.

854
01:04:58,603 --> 01:05:00,647
Not a good time.
I'm heading into a meeting.

855
01:05:00,980 --> 01:05:04,067
<i>Okay, I'll send it.
Clear something up for me.</i>

856
01:05:04,484 --> 01:05:06,611
<i>The first trip, Fitz Roy, remember?</i>

857
01:05:07,195 --> 01:05:09,572
<i>When Malacara
fell into the frozen lake,</i>

858
01:05:09,656 --> 01:05:13,368
<i>the hair dryer you used,
was it yours or from the campsite?</i>

859
01:05:13,451 --> 01:05:15,036
<i>The hair dryer, remember?</i>

860
01:05:16,037 --> 01:05:18,373
No, it was my sister's
and she still complains.

861
01:05:18,748 --> 01:05:21,292
Malacara was so scared
he chewed it all up.

862
01:05:23,128 --> 01:05:25,296
<i>Yes. I remember.</i>

863
01:05:25,380 --> 01:05:27,340
- <i>Poor thing.</i>
- Poor thing.

864
01:05:27,424 --> 01:05:29,217
<i>Listen... Doorbell, Mechi.</i>

865
01:05:29,300 --> 01:05:31,302
<i>They're here for the computers I sold.</i>

866
01:05:31,386 --> 01:05:33,555
<i>I'll send the text,
check it and let me know.</i>

867
01:05:33,638 --> 01:05:38,059
<i>The investor presentation is at 9:00 AM.
No, 10:00 AM.</i>

868
01:05:38,143 --> 01:05:41,396
<i>I don't recall if it was 09:00 or 10:00.
Please, I hope you come, okay?</i>

869
01:05:41,479 --> 01:05:43,314
- <i>Kiss.</i>
- Tell Frida I'm not going...

870
01:05:47,485 --> 01:05:49,487
- Is it good?
- It's spicy.

871
01:05:49,571 --> 01:05:50,780
- Spicy?
- Yes.

872
01:05:53,700 --> 01:05:55,660
No, thanks. Enjoy.

873
01:05:59,706 --> 01:06:00,707
Tasty, right?

874
01:06:05,044 --> 01:06:07,714
How is it? Is it good? Do you like it?

875
01:06:08,715 --> 01:06:10,008
Came out well.

876
01:06:15,597 --> 01:06:16,681
Anyone want some?

877
01:06:17,682 --> 01:06:19,267
- No?
- No, that's enough.

878
01:06:19,350 --> 01:06:20,351
Okay.

879
01:06:36,242 --> 01:06:37,243
Did you rest?

880
01:06:39,078 --> 01:06:41,206
Yes.

881
01:06:44,667 --> 01:06:45,668
Sit down.

882
01:06:54,719 --> 01:06:57,472
Alejandra, my wife. A friend.

883
01:06:57,555 --> 01:07:00,266
- Hello, nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you. Guillermo.

884
01:07:01,392 --> 01:07:02,727
Enjoy.

885
01:07:03,061 --> 01:07:04,437
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

886
01:07:09,025 --> 01:07:12,070
Why aren't you sleeping?
Something bothering you?

887
01:07:14,572 --> 01:07:16,074
Yes, many things.

888
01:07:22,121 --> 01:07:23,456
It's...

889
01:07:24,082 --> 01:07:26,668
I've got a lot of work,
a lot of demand...

890
01:07:29,587 --> 01:07:31,506
Not for the work itself, but for...

891
01:07:33,633 --> 01:07:35,051
my presence.

892
01:07:35,593 --> 01:07:39,097
- What do you do?
- I solve problems.

893
01:07:39,597 --> 01:07:43,393
- Problems?
- Yes. In a big company.

894
01:07:45,520 --> 01:07:46,563
And...

895
01:07:49,315 --> 01:07:53,486
And that mixed
with several things, and with the...

896
01:07:55,405 --> 01:07:56,364
The...?

897
01:07:56,447 --> 01:07:58,700
Well, this buzzing.

898
01:07:59,450 --> 01:08:04,122
That thing... sometimes it's there,
sometimes not.

899
01:08:05,290 --> 01:08:08,251
But mostly there.

900
01:08:10,003 --> 01:08:11,004
Did you get checked?

901
01:08:12,297 --> 01:08:13,339
Yeah, everything.

902
01:08:14,132 --> 01:08:18,136
All the tests.
And they say I've got nothing.

903
01:08:19,554 --> 01:08:23,433
Everything.
I even went to Houston.

904
01:08:23,516 --> 01:08:24,642
- Houston?
- Yes.

905
01:08:26,227 --> 01:08:30,356
- And? Did it help?
- I saw the specialist, the top one.

906
01:08:30,440 --> 01:08:35,445
The one who charges a fortune,
and nothing. He said I've got nothing.

907
01:08:36,154 --> 01:08:37,655
Everyone says I've got nothing.

908
01:08:38,072 --> 01:08:40,158
So, a fortune just to be told

909
01:08:40,241 --> 01:08:41,534
- that you've got nothing.
- I've got nothing.

910
01:08:54,505 --> 01:08:56,007
BARBIE LAWYER
VOICE MESSAGE

911
01:08:56,549 --> 01:09:01,054
<i>Mechi, I'm traveling on Monday.
Please let me know. Thanks and regards.</i>

912
01:09:16,235 --> 01:09:19,989
<i>Mechi, can you confirm
you got my last message? Kiss.</i>

913
01:09:20,657 --> 01:09:22,617
Enough. I want to see the damn video.

914
01:09:26,663 --> 01:09:28,164
There she goes again.

915
01:09:45,723 --> 01:09:47,225
But disconnected how?

916
01:09:48,434 --> 01:09:49,560
Good...

917
01:09:50,228 --> 01:09:54,273
It's like... a mix of things, right?
Never just one.

918
01:09:54,357 --> 01:09:56,317
It's... I don't know.

919
01:09:56,401 --> 01:10:00,363
For example, some years ago
we went to Monterrey,

920
01:10:00,738 --> 01:10:02,573
since her dad's family is from there.

921
01:10:03,032 --> 01:10:06,494
They've got an amazing hacienda
in La Huasteca, like a fantasy place.

922
01:10:06,577 --> 01:10:08,037
Amazing. Beautiful.

923
01:10:08,621 --> 01:10:10,331
And we all went, right?

924
01:10:10,415 --> 01:10:14,502
Like 50 people,
daily activities, even breakfast.

925
01:10:15,086 --> 01:10:18,756
And I was training for a half marathon.

926
01:10:19,424 --> 01:10:24,220
So after breakfast
I say goodbye and go running, right?

927
01:10:25,054 --> 01:10:29,392
I go out and say, "Damn, I'm so happy."

928
01:10:29,475 --> 01:10:33,438
I start to feel
like my legs are getting heavy,

929
01:10:33,521 --> 01:10:37,400
and suddenly, I don't know,
nature, running, the air...

930
01:10:37,483 --> 01:10:41,279
It all starts making me feel
like everything's going to be okay.

931
01:10:41,612 --> 01:10:44,449
I start feeling happy.
I think I even start singing.

932
01:10:45,283 --> 01:10:47,493
And when I change direction...

933
01:10:48,077 --> 01:10:53,416
Knee's gone. Like gum snapping. Snap!

934
01:10:53,499 --> 01:10:55,293
- But running?
- Yes.

935
01:10:55,376 --> 01:10:56,753
I swore I'd torn my knee.

936
01:10:57,170 --> 01:11:00,715
But no. I stretch it and realize...

937
01:11:01,048 --> 01:11:05,553
When I put weight on it...
Terrible pain! It swells.

938
01:11:05,636 --> 01:11:11,100
So I head back, right?
Dragging myself. Bad. Like...

939
01:11:11,642 --> 01:11:14,687
I said: "Someone's going to come
pick me up at some point."

940
01:11:15,480 --> 01:11:20,985
But no, nobody came.
It took me five hours to get back.

941
01:11:21,068 --> 01:11:23,070
And when I arrived, my wife said:

942
01:11:23,154 --> 01:11:25,239
"What's up,
we've been waiting for you here."

943
01:11:25,323 --> 01:11:28,993
"What do you mean you're waiting?
Didn't it occur to you to come get me?"

944
01:11:29,076 --> 01:11:30,745
They told me to put some ice on it.

945
01:11:31,078 --> 01:11:34,207
And the following week I found out
I had torn my ACL.

946
01:11:34,290 --> 01:11:38,669
I don't know, it's just...
Things like that.

947
01:11:39,086 --> 01:11:44,592
Coming from different backgrounds.
And they see it another way.

948
01:11:45,218 --> 01:11:47,553
I come from a very small family.

949
01:11:49,138 --> 01:11:53,226
A dad who works every day,
who cries when he gets drunk.

950
01:11:53,684 --> 01:11:56,521
A mom who finds it so hard
to leave the house.

951
01:11:57,605 --> 01:12:00,149
I've got a brother
who struggles with life.

952
01:12:01,234 --> 01:12:03,611
Poor guy,
everything he does goes wrong.

953
01:12:05,530 --> 01:12:10,535
So when I met Javiera,
suddenly I was welcomed

954
01:12:10,618 --> 01:12:16,415
into this safe place
where they give you everything.

955
01:12:17,041 --> 01:12:19,460
They gave us the house,
they gave us the cars,

956
01:12:19,544 --> 01:12:23,756
they gave us everything,
even, and this hurts to admit,

957
01:12:25,132 --> 01:12:29,470
the position I have at Alicabo,
I think I owe it to my father-in-law.

958
01:12:31,681 --> 01:12:35,768
Yeah, well, you know.
I'm really angry, honestly.

959
01:13:05,590 --> 01:13:10,595
I love that thing couples have,
being quiet but still okay.

960
01:13:12,513 --> 01:13:13,723
Maybe they're fighting.

961
01:13:18,603 --> 01:13:22,273
And you with your wife, no connection?
I don't mean daily stuff.

962
01:13:22,356 --> 01:13:24,191
With Kato I have Google Calendar.

963
01:13:24,275 --> 01:13:26,444
He doesn't check it,
but he still loses the password.

964
01:13:27,153 --> 01:13:32,033
I mean more honest, deeper talks.

965
01:13:33,117 --> 01:13:35,036
Complicity,
being on each other's radar.

966
01:13:37,496 --> 01:13:39,248
No. Honestly, no.

967
01:13:41,459 --> 01:13:44,670
- But you talk about Kato all the time.
- I don't talk. I complain.

968
01:13:44,754 --> 01:13:45,755
I complain all the time.

969
01:13:46,380 --> 01:13:47,381
Do you fight a lot?

970
01:13:53,429 --> 01:13:54,430
I envy that.

971
01:13:57,725 --> 01:13:59,352
I just can't understand him.

972
01:13:59,435 --> 01:14:02,229
What used to make me laugh
now irritates me.

973
01:14:02,313 --> 01:14:04,023
I don't know, I lost my patience.

974
01:14:04,440 --> 01:14:07,318
I hear him speak in public
and I'm embarrassed.

975
01:14:11,739 --> 01:14:15,326
Still, I envy his ability
to be optimistic.

976
01:14:17,119 --> 01:14:18,621
He believes in himself.
He's failed many times,

977
01:14:18,704 --> 01:14:20,331
yet he still believes.
And he believes in me.

978
01:14:21,290 --> 01:14:22,291
More than I do.

979
01:14:23,084 --> 01:14:24,168
And that kills me.

980
01:14:34,387 --> 01:14:35,513
And does he want to separate?

981
01:14:36,305 --> 01:14:38,516
He says yes,
but even that he postpones.

982
01:14:38,599 --> 01:14:41,394
His mother's illness, the move,
Frida's birthday.

983
01:14:41,477 --> 01:14:43,396
And I take care
of his mother's illness,

984
01:14:43,479 --> 01:14:45,690
the move, Frida's birthday,
the family finances,

985
01:14:46,023 --> 01:14:47,274
and now even the separation.

986
01:14:51,237 --> 01:14:52,571
And who does Frida look like?

987
01:14:52,655 --> 01:14:55,408
- Physically like me, I'm gorgeous.
- Sure.

988
01:14:55,491 --> 01:14:56,450
Yes.

989
01:14:56,534 --> 01:14:59,537
And personality too, she's like me.
Moody like her mother.

990
01:15:00,538 --> 01:15:02,373
In the morning you can't talk to her.

991
01:15:06,544 --> 01:15:08,212
Dreamy like her father.

992
01:15:10,006 --> 01:15:11,716
Super persistent with what she likes.

993
01:15:12,299 --> 01:15:14,176
Very smart, but...

994
01:15:16,554 --> 01:15:17,596
inconsistent.

995
01:15:29,108 --> 01:15:32,069
Sorry.
I can't stop talking about myself.

996
01:15:33,404 --> 01:15:34,447
Tell me about your son.

997
01:15:35,114 --> 01:15:36,115
What's he like?

998
01:15:36,532 --> 01:15:37,616
- Chemita?
- Yes.

999
01:15:39,410 --> 01:15:42,038
Well, Chemita isn't like me,

1000
01:15:43,330 --> 01:15:47,126
but he's the coolest kid.

1001
01:15:47,752 --> 01:15:49,253
He's such a good person.

1002
01:15:50,254 --> 01:15:51,255
Look.

1003
01:15:52,590 --> 01:15:54,592
I told you they gave him a boat, right?

1004
01:15:54,675 --> 01:15:56,093
- His grandfather.
- Yes.

1005
01:15:56,177 --> 01:15:58,262
Well, here it is. They sent me this.

1006
01:15:59,055 --> 01:16:01,390
Look, here's the grandfather.
Here's the boat.

1007
01:16:01,474 --> 01:16:03,225
And they're in their first regatta.

1008
01:16:03,684 --> 01:16:07,563
And if they finish top four,
they qualify for something...

1009
01:16:07,646 --> 01:16:09,190
I don't even know what.

1010
01:16:09,273 --> 01:16:11,233
- But this is now?
- Yes, this is now.

1011
01:16:11,317 --> 01:16:12,610
And what are you doing here?

1012
01:16:14,195 --> 01:16:15,196
- What?
- Sorry to intrude,

1013
01:16:15,279 --> 01:16:18,074
but why aren't you there?
What are you doing here?

1014
01:16:20,659 --> 01:16:23,079
Well... same as you.

1015
01:16:30,711 --> 01:16:32,004
You know what I read once?

1016
01:16:33,214 --> 01:16:36,550
You choose your first partner
for differences,

1017
01:16:36,634 --> 01:16:41,514
and the second for similarities,
for what you share.

1018
01:16:42,515 --> 01:16:43,599
- Bravo.
- Bravo.

1019
01:16:43,682 --> 01:16:46,227
Yes, I like that.

1020
01:16:48,145 --> 01:16:49,396
- Let me see.
- What?

1021
01:16:52,650 --> 01:16:55,402
- We have to learn to choose better.
- Yes.

1022
01:16:58,155 --> 01:16:59,156
Luis!

1023
01:17:08,165 --> 01:17:09,708
It'll sound crazy,

1024
01:17:10,042 --> 01:17:13,504
but tonight my husband and I
celebrate 20 years of marriage.

1025
01:17:14,004 --> 01:17:16,674
Twenty years, through good times
and not so good.

1026
01:17:17,007 --> 01:17:18,175
Through the good. Yes.

1027
01:17:18,259 --> 01:17:20,719
And as you may have noticed,
we really love oysters.

1028
01:17:21,053 --> 01:17:22,346
- Big oysters.
- Big oysters.

1029
01:17:22,429 --> 01:17:25,307
And so, we wanted to ask
if you'd be so kind

1030
01:17:25,391 --> 01:17:28,227
as to let us join you fishing tonight.

1031
01:17:30,229 --> 01:17:31,522
No.

1032
01:17:42,283 --> 01:17:45,661
Years from now you'll be reading
a story to your grandkids.

1033
01:17:46,453 --> 01:17:48,289
And in one of the drawings

1034
01:17:50,166 --> 01:17:53,043
there'll be a child swimming alone
under the moonlight.

1035
01:17:54,128 --> 01:17:55,713
And you'll see yourself in him.

1036
01:17:59,049 --> 01:18:04,722
And you'll feel so good for having done
something you never imagined you could.

1037
01:18:07,558 --> 01:18:10,102
You'll want to tell it,
but you'll keep it,

1038
01:18:10,186 --> 01:18:11,687
because no one would believe you.

1039
01:18:20,070 --> 01:18:21,405
But holding hands, okay?

1040
01:18:22,031 --> 01:18:23,032
Yes?

1041
01:18:57,274 --> 01:18:59,109
Okay.

1042
01:19:03,322 --> 01:19:05,157
- We just jump in like that?
- Yes, sir.

1043
01:19:05,241 --> 01:19:06,533
- Like that?
- Yes, please.

1044
01:19:11,455 --> 01:19:12,456
Ready?

1045
01:19:12,998 --> 01:19:13,999
Let's go.

1046
01:20:05,342 --> 01:20:08,345
I think we laugh too much
for being married 20 years, don't we?

1047
01:20:14,393 --> 01:20:19,315
Hey, I just got the official offer
to be Alicabo's new global CEO.

1048
01:20:21,191 --> 01:20:23,360
I've got a call
with the board tomorrow.

1049
01:20:26,405 --> 01:20:27,740
And what does your family say?

1050
01:20:28,615 --> 01:20:31,035
They're thrilled.
They want me to accept.

1051
01:20:43,130 --> 01:20:45,049
What if I make you regional manager?

1052
01:20:46,550 --> 01:20:48,552
No, this isn't for me.

1053
01:20:48,635 --> 01:20:51,638
I thought I could, but no.
It's too much.

1054
01:21:04,318 --> 01:21:07,237
Hello. Are you alone?

1055
01:21:07,654 --> 01:21:09,490
Hello. It's beautiful!

1056
01:21:10,491 --> 01:21:11,492
Hello.

1057
01:21:13,410 --> 01:21:14,411
Is he alone?

1058
01:21:36,433 --> 01:21:37,434
What's up?

1059
01:22:37,578 --> 01:22:40,664
I've got three of these
that I will just break, you know?

1060
01:22:40,747 --> 01:22:42,082
- Yeah.
- Break them.

1061
01:22:42,166 --> 01:22:43,167
And...

1062
01:22:43,667 --> 01:22:45,419
This is a "bye, Alicabo."

1063
01:22:45,502 --> 01:22:48,464
- No.
- Michelle, yes.

1064
01:22:48,547 --> 01:22:51,258
- They want to talk to you.
- No, it's ok.

1065
01:22:51,341 --> 01:22:52,551
I'll call them.

1066
01:22:52,634 --> 01:22:54,553
No, Guillermo. Think about it.

1067
01:22:54,636 --> 01:22:55,596
Thanks for everything.

1068
01:22:55,679 --> 01:22:57,556
Let's wish each other good luck.

1069
01:22:58,307 --> 01:23:00,642
- Speak soon, yeah?
- Good luck.

1070
01:23:05,647 --> 01:23:06,648
That's it.

1071
01:23:09,526 --> 01:23:12,029
Now they have to talk to HR,

1072
01:23:12,112 --> 01:23:14,656
then their lawyers
talk to my lawyer and that's it.

1073
01:23:16,408 --> 01:23:18,619
Offers pour in for people over 45.

1074
01:23:32,049 --> 01:23:33,050
For Frida.

1075
01:23:36,386 --> 01:23:37,387
Thank you.

1076
01:23:41,725 --> 01:23:44,269
Maybe we'll get lucky
and end up in the same cell.

1077
01:24:13,715 --> 01:24:16,009
Come on. Come!

1078
01:24:17,094 --> 01:24:18,095
Come.

1079
01:25:18,071 --> 01:25:19,197
DIVORCE PAPERS

1080
01:25:22,367 --> 01:25:24,077
DOCUMENT SIGNED SUCCESSFULLY.

1081
01:26:17,089 --> 01:26:19,299
What are you doing here?

1082
01:26:24,054 --> 01:26:25,055
And that dog?

1083
01:26:31,687 --> 01:26:32,729
Where did he come from?

1084
01:26:33,355 --> 01:26:36,566
Well, from life itself.
His name's Roña.

1085
01:26:37,067 --> 01:26:39,444
...nothing more than an excuse
to celebrate.

1086
01:26:41,405 --> 01:26:46,368
Don't you feel you think of family
differently now? The concept changed.

1087
01:26:47,327 --> 01:26:50,414
Changed how we treat each other,
even how we love each other

1088
01:26:50,747 --> 01:26:52,040
and who's included.

1089
01:26:52,124 --> 01:26:56,044
Our dogs, our cats, our parrots,
our turtles... They're family.

1090
01:26:56,378 --> 01:27:01,007
Look, I'm not exaggerating
when I say Malacara taught us

1091
01:27:01,091 --> 01:27:03,552
to be parents
before Frida was born.

1092
01:27:03,635 --> 01:27:04,636
I swear.

1093
01:27:06,346 --> 01:27:11,226
This isn't just an app
for our dogs to have sex.

1094
01:27:11,309 --> 01:27:13,603
Do we want it as a business?
Sure. But it's about...

1095
01:27:13,687 --> 01:27:15,105
How's it going?

1096
01:27:16,648 --> 01:27:19,484
That bald guy with glasses
already checked the time twice,

1097
01:27:19,568 --> 01:27:21,153
so... I don't know.

1098
01:27:36,710 --> 01:27:38,420
- Do I just pull it like that?
- Yes.

1099
01:27:38,503 --> 01:27:40,130
Just like that, but harder.

1100
01:27:42,090 --> 01:27:43,091
Alright!